Chapter: E1000Match
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Kernel chapter E1000e
  cites Kernel chapter Pci

 What this test covers and what it does NOT.

 There is no e1000 device under codex-vm -- the only NIC it emulates is
 an ISA NE2000 -- so nothing here touches a register, a descriptor ring
 or a frame. Every function in E1000e that reads or writes the device is
 UNTESTED and stays untested until the driver meets real hardware. This
 file pins the part of the driver that is decidable without the part:
 which PCI devices it claims, and the alignment arithmetic its rings
 depend on.

 Saying so matters more than the rows below. A green result here is
 evidence about device selection and nothing else, and reading it as
 evidence the driver works would be the exact failure this project keeps
 recording.

 The negative rows are the test. A matcher that answered True to
 everything would pass a positive-only suite, so each of the three ways
 a device can fail to be ours gets its own row: wrong vendor, wrong
 class, wrong subclass. The expected values are written as literals
 rather than computed, because a judge built out of the subject cannot
 fail with it.

Section: Fixtures

  mk : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> PciDevice
  mk (vendor) (did) (cls) (sub) =
    PciDevice { pci-bus = 0, pci-dev = 0, pci-func = 0, pci-vendor = __narrow vendor, pci-device-id = __narrow did, pci-class = __narrow cls, pci-subclass = __narrow sub, pci-header-type = 0 }

 Each fixture carries its OWN device id so that find-present names which
 device was selected rather than merely that something was. With one id
 shared across the fixtures, a matcher that claimed every device would
 still answer find-present correctly, and the row would be decoration.

  intel-eth : PciDevice
  intel-eth = mk 32902 5560 2 0

  realtek-eth : PciDevice
  realtek-eth = mk 4332 33625 2 0

  intel-storage : PciDevice
  intel-storage = mk 32902 41112 1 6

  intel-other-net : PciDevice
  intel-other-net = mk 32902 4181 2 128

Section: BAR Window Fixtures

 The two failing addresses are measured rather than invented: OVMF was
 observed placing a NIC BAR at 0x81060000, which is below the mapped
 device window and inside the heap and stack arena, and placing an xHCI
 window above four gigabytes, where nothing is mapped. 0xF7C00000 stands
 for the case that works.

  bar-at : Integer, Boolean -> PciBar
  bar-at (base) (io) =
    PciBar { bar-index = 0, bar-base = base, bar-is-io = io, bar-is-64bit = False }

Section: Judges

  yn : Boolean -> Text
  yn (b) = if b then "T" else "F"

  found : PciScanResult -> Text
  found (scan) =
    when e1000-find scan
      is Just (d) -> show (d.pci-device-id)
      is None -> "none"

  scan-of : List PciDevice -> PciScanResult
  scan-of (ds) = PciScanResult { devices = ds, count = list-length ds }

 e1000-poll-raw is the entry the network stack calls, and its absent
 guard is the only part of it reachable without a device: a zero window
 must answer no-frame rather than reading descriptor memory at zero.

  poll-raw-hit : Integer -> Boolean
  poll-raw-hit (mmio) =
    let r = e1000-poll-raw mmio 0 0 0
    in r.r-has-frame

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("intel-eth=" & yn (e1000-is-candidate intel-eth))
    print-line-uni ("realtek-eth=" & yn (e1000-is-candidate realtek-eth))
    print-line-uni ("intel-storage=" & yn (e1000-is-candidate intel-storage))
    print-line-uni ("intel-other-net=" & yn (e1000-is-candidate intel-other-net))
    print-line-uni ("find-present=" & found (scan-of [realtek-eth, intel-eth]))
    print-line-uni ("find-absent=" & found (scan-of [realtek-eth, intel-storage]))
    print-line-uni ("align-0=" & show (e1000-align 0 16))
    print-line-uni ("align-1=" & show (e1000-align 1 16))
    print-line-uni ("align-16=" & show (e1000-align 16 16))
    print-line-uni ("align-17=" & show (e1000-align 17 16))
    print-line-uni ("align-4095=" & show (e1000-align 4095 16))
    print-line-uni ("tx-cmd=" & show e1000-tx-cmd-all)
    print-line-uni ("bar-in-window=" & show (e1000-bar-verdict (bar-at 4156555264 False)))
    print-line-uni ("bar-ovmf-nic=" & show (e1000-bar-verdict (bar-at 2164326400 False)))
    print-line-uni ("bar-above-4g=" & show (e1000-bar-verdict (bar-at 4294967296 False)))
    print-line-uni ("bar-window-lo=" & show (e1000-bar-verdict (bar-at 3221225472 False)))
    print-line-uni ("bar-window-top=" & show (e1000-bar-verdict (bar-at 4294967295 False)))
    print-line-uni ("bar-io=" & show (e1000-bar-verdict (bar-at 49152 True)))
    print-line-uni ("bar-zero=" & show (e1000-bar-verdict (bar-at 0 False)))
    print-line-uni ("poll-raw-absent=" & yn (poll-raw-hit 0))
  end

